WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:07.360
<i>There was someone who remained 
alive in Akari's memories.</i>

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.280
<i>There was someone who 
taught Michelle strength.</i>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.070
<i>That is why they fought.</i>

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.620
<i>That is why they could not die.</i>

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.910
<i>The fight seemed to end, but...</i>

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.360
I believe in you, Alex.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.820
I'm gonna come back as 
a ghost and haunt you!

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.230
That was definitely on 
course to be a strike.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.110
But the bat curved at a weird time...

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.830
And there hasn't been a second missile.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.990
Hunter's Net

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:17.840
Why?

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.070
Does that mean the mission was a success?

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.400
We succeeded in making them waste a missile,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.460
but we failed to create a big smoke signal.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.710
So I guess we half-succeeded.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.120
Alex!

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.230
I've found the First and the Second.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.450
Retrieving.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.350
It's been a while, XO Davis.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.480
No. 4 Division, Rank 50, Bao Zhilan.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:58.400
Some things have happened, so I'm taking 
you and Hizamaru-kun into custody.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.960
That's an airbike.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.560
How long have you been following us?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.410
You two must be in a lot of pain.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.960
Wow, you've both broken your lower jaws.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.680
Same with the left clavicle.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.020
Ribs, of course.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.750
And you've hit your head hard.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:21.040
The XO probably has a lot of 
fractures in her skull too, right?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.010
You're so badly injured it's amazing you 
have the strength left to glare at me.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.600
The drugs really ran out 
at just the right time.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.230
Now...

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.630
The Second and the First are secured.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.030
I've also acquired 200 samples 
captured by the US-Japan Division.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:46.950
Nice, huh?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.840
Please just stay there.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.540
Not that you could move if you wanted to.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.530
What happened to Captain Komachi?

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.330
I don't know.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.460
Don't you screw with us!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.800
I'm not giving you any information.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.220
And I'm the one asking the questions here.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.810
It was really difficult, you know.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:11.060
We didn't know who was 
on board Unit 1 and 2.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.920
Was it really you two?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.840
We wanted you alive, if possible.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.030
But there was another one, right?

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.320
A low-ranked girl.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.890
She contacted us from Unit 2.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.450
And Rank 12 is here too, right?

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.250
Don't worry.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.860
We won't kill them if we don't have to.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.920
They're part of our team, after all.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.880
So, first question.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.120
Unit 1 was unmanned.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.770
Where did the rest of 
No. 1 and No. 2 Divisions go?

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.430
They're all dead.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.900
We fought the terraformars twice 
before we ran into the Paraponera.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:03.900
Then...

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.530
Hey!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.910
You bastard...

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.050
Oh?

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.890
You feel pain, then?

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.720
Even after the way you were born?

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.300
You have guts.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.970
Where are the others?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.870
Where are Rank 8 and Rank 9?

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.470
Give us your orders, XO Michelle.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.150
How can we win?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.480
There are two ways to beat No. 4 Division: 
the direct way, and the indirect way.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.480
You guys have to...

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.460
Where are the noncombatants 
from No. 1 and No. 2 Divisions?

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:51.960
Oh, dear.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.360
Is it that time already?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.710
You two just stay there, okay?

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.920
I've secured the First and the Second.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.750
Requesting pickup, General Liu.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.920
Roger.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.800
We're on our way.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.810
I'll start heading back with Unit 1,

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.460
but I don't see any other personnel 
from No. 1 and No. 2 Divisions.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.190
Their whereabouts remain unknown.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.410
It's almost night.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.770
Yeah. Our job is to defeat 
No. 4 Division indirectly.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.890
Yeah. Our job is to defeat 
No. 4 Division indirectly.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.270
Your job is to return the communications 
tower they're using as a jammer to normal,

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:37.000
and let the Earth know that 
No. 4 Division has betrayed us.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.360
That will make all the 
branches on Earth take action,

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.960
and allow us to defeat them indirectly.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.450
You okay, Peggy?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.680
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 82
Peggy Fortie
US-Japan Joint No. 2 Division
Surgery Base: Short-Beaked Echidna</b>

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:55.850
Jared, how much is left?

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.880
We're past the mines.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.710
500 meters to Annex 1.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.800
500 meters, huh?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.400
Let me take a little break.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.020
Okay.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:05.860
Sorry.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.620
I don't blame you.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.050
Even if you've got the hands and 
strength of a short-beaked echidna,

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.230
you're a girl, and a non-combatant.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.170
Yeah.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.870
And we shouldn't go up to the surface yet.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.830
Why, Wolf?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.240
A huge number of biomagnetic 
fields just disappeared.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.250
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 90
Wolf Redfield
US-Japan Joint No. 2 Division
Surgery Base: Hammerhead Shark</b>

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:25.180
It's possible it was either poison gas, 
a biological weapon, or radiation,

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.060
but not a nuclear explosion.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:27.960
They...

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.800
They've got something like that?

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:30.860
Yeah.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.890
First 500 biomagnetic fields rushed the area,

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.830
probably terraformars.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.640
Then the second they got close 
to the Annex 1 they all disappeared.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:41.950
Most of them died instantly.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.030
I didn't feel anything.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:47.010
Your surgery base is a killer 
whale, so you use sound waves.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.080
But mine is a hammerhead shark.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:52.350
I detect the biomagnetic fields 
generated by living creatures.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.030
I'm sure of it.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:57.660
No. 4 Division used some kind of NBC weapon.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.160
Then we can't get close, can we?

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.040
No, we will. We have to.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:09.570
That's the reason non-combatant engineers 
like us came all the way to this planet.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.820
Wow, Rank 90, you're really talking tough.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.140
What?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.450
You got a plan?

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.040
It's unlikely to be radiation.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.810
So we wait until dawn.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:21.850
Dawn?

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:25.700
Any remaining bacteria will be disabled 
by the change in the amount of sunlight.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.450
Any poison gas will be blown away.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.200
If we can just distract them

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:34.050
for a couple of minutes to 
a few dozen seconds at sunrise,

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.320
we should be able to get inside 
the Annex 1 control room.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.140
There, we'll hack the tower that 
No. 4 Division is controlling.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:46.190
It was our job as engineers to 
set the thing up originally.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:52.170
And then we tell the Earth that 
No. 4 Division has betrayed them.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.680
Don't underestimate civilians.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.150
I've had all kinds of terrible 
experiences at crappy companies.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.340
Sorry for being an asshole back there.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.600
I'm counting on you.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.960
Yeah.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:09.180
But really, all I'm good for is knowing 
things and taking problems seriously.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.770
I can't do anything against 
the terraformars,

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.410
but I want to protect 
my teammates, you know?

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.770
Akira-kun and XO Michelle have 
always been the primary targets,

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.810
but they've always protected 
us so we wouldn't be killed.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.790
And Alex and Yaeko-chan, too...

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.610
So I want to do something to help, as well.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:32.500
Even if they're not cut out for 
combat, I'd like to use our powers.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.870
Yeah.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:35.920
I'd like to protect them.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.370
<i>Sheila.</i>

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.460
I'm sorry!

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.900
I-I was with her, and Sheila still...

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.110
Sheila...

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.980
What did we come all the way to Mars to do?

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.210
To protect Sheila—

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.000
Yeah?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.550
Then you don't need to apologize to me.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.430
Because that's not why I'm here.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:23.150
We've been used no matter what, 
ever since we were born.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.070
We could join a gang, sell ourselves,

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.270
or do nothing and stay trash.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.940
We came here to change that life, didn't we?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.990
And you're the same, right?

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:35.500
You don't have time to sit there and cry!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.620
I'm taking vengeance for Sheila.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.030
Yeah...

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.250
And... I don't know if 
this is possible, but...

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.690
If this isn't a weapon, but a bacteria-type 
or some other ability that someone's using,

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.730
they're going to be military, obviously.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:01.510
If that's the case, it's up to you.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:02.720
Got it.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:02.720
Yeah.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.050
Stay safe, everyone.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:10.100
We'll defeat those traitors in No. 4 
Division and all go back to Earth.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:23.850
Damn it!

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.680
The terraformars have already found us...

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.450
That was a signal!

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.460
Those two found us and 
were just delaying us.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:37.670
I thought that all the unique weapons 
would have powerful security on them.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:41.380
But they've set it up so that teammates 
can use them at times like these?

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.780
We can't go any faster?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.820
This is an old model.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:04.320
We'll never catch up to Michelle 
and Akari at this rate.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:06.350
It's almost nightfall.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.250
Yeah. And it's gonna be a different 
night than we've had before.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.040
Be ready for combat.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:16.250
This is the second time after the first 
night that it's their time to attack.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:20.590
And tonight they've evolved 
even more over the past week.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.610
We're getting through this, Hizamaru-kun.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.130
I'm taking you home alive.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:33.000
<b>Airbike
A small flying craft for use in Plan Alpha.
Capable of traveling both on the ground and in the air.
Normally used for transport and rescue.
Can't even go half as fast as 
the high-speed escape pods.</b>

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.700
Th-This is crazy!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.660
He's insane!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.620
What is he thinking?

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.900
Why isn't he transforming?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.150
<i>He doesn't have any combat powers?</i>

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.680
<i>But then what are these 
strong physical abilities?</i>

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.350
They aren't the movements of someone 
who practices swordsmanship.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.610
Even if he does have some kind of 
mysterious power, there are too many.

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:21.200
There are thousands of them!

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.530
This is impossible!

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.240
Yeah, maybe.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.290
So I'm going to use them as a decoy.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.740
The terraformars have a priority 
list for everything they target.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.370
First is people using tools, 
or tools themselves.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:44.030
Preferably expensive tools.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:46.190
Second is people who are alone.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.220
Third is people who are injured.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.810
And fourth, for some reason 
they go after women.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.200
N-No!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.830
Yaeko!

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:07.990
Alex!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:07.990
Yaeko!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.950
We don't know why they go after women.

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.450
We know it's not for the purpose of sex.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.580
But, for some reason, they seem drawn to them.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.880
Stop it, you bastard!

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.310
A-Alex...

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:27.470
You... Why...

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:29.970
You aren't transformed!

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.680
Why? Come on...

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.430
I don't know...

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:39.360
I know if I can't transform 
I'll just get in the way.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:40.560
Weird, huh?

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:46.670
Maybe I wanted to show off 
because you were watching...

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.630
Back when you...

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.620
You didn't come back and 
I was getting worried.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:57.760
Yeah.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.970
They're not coming.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.160
Yeah.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.270
I'm sorry about Sheila-chan.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:18.600
Yeah.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.150
She was a good girl, huh?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.420
Yeah.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.550
She did all she could, I heard.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:24.770
Yeah.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:28.830
But...

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:31.550
She shouldn't have come to Mars.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.370
I didn't see it,

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.080
but even if someone was there they 
probably couldn't have saved her.

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.620
And when I think about that it 
makes a lot of sense to me.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:48.030
It feels like, for some reason,

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:55.380
I lost the desire to complain about the fact 
that no one's coming to help us a long time ago.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.340
That's because you're the big brother.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.560
For Sheila and Marcos.

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:03.730
Big brother...?

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.280
You're the oldest of the three of you,

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:10.480
and you've helped Marcos 
and us on Mars, but...

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.550
There are people here who will help you.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:15.960
Yeah.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.750
You're right.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.770
XO Michelle, Captain Komachi,

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.730
Akari...

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:22.660
And...

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.120
And?

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.530
You?!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.050
When you heard that Sheila-chan died,

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.450
you forced yourself to hold back, right?

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.840
It's okay to cry when 
you're hurting, you know?

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.930
The XO said that.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.790
Cry when you're sad. Howl when you're angry.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:45.970
And when that's done, tell a joke and laugh.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:49.480
Your big brother and big sister are here.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.200
Now cry,

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.660
against your big sister's huge chest.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.950
We've got a great deal 
going on! Only 5000 yen!

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:57.820
Huh?

00:16:58.270 --> 00:16:59.520
Did that not work?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.980
Okay, then 4000 yen...

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:05.200
Wait, I'm not following this.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.520
Who's my big sister?

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:08.310
Huh?

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.230
Alex, you're 18, aren't you?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.090
What?

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.670
You're older than me?!

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:13.760
That's right!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.880
I'm 20! All grown up!

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.440
Seriously?

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.330
You're older than me?

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.260
How rude!

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:27.900
You thought I was younger than you?

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:28.690
Yeah.

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:30.730
Less mature, too.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:34.400
What? I'm older, and I'm more mature!

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:37.720
My M.A.R.S. Ranking is lower, though...

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:50.290
That's right...

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:57.240
I just kind of leapt out without thinking.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.820
Sorry, Yaeko.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.180
Don't worry about me. Run.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.390
You've got your drugs, right?

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.890
If you can transform and 
get out of here somehow...

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.850
It's okay, Alex.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.360
It's okay.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.070
There's someone here...

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.700
...who will protect you!

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.870
No, Yaeko!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:32.450
You smell good. Did you know that?

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.880
I smell good?

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:38.820
I have the smell of a slum garbage 
dump that will never go away.

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.260
No, that's not true.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.220
You smell like the sun.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.850
Induce transformation!

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.370
Yaeko...?

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.360
I'm the one who stinks.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.870
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 98
Yanasegawa Yaeko
No. 2 Division
Striped Skunk</b>

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:08.750
M.A.R.S. Ranking 98,

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.760
Surgery base, striped skunk!

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:13.520
Well?

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:14.670
Stinky, huh?

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:17.860
Get any closer and I'll 
make it even stinkier!

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.440
Come on, while they're wary of the smell...

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:22.800
Y-Yeah.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.260
You're amazing, Yaeko.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.000
Wow.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.510
Y-Yeah?

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.100
Amazingly smelly.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.000
Yaeko, are you pissing yourself?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.200
I am not...

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.340
Just a little...

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:38.040
Wait, no. This is how this power works!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:43.040
It smells like a mix between garlic and 
rotten eggs and a bunch of other awful things.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:45.980
I'm glad you're a bird with 
a bad sense of smell.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:47.070
But it stinks.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.330
<b>But It
 Stinks</b>

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.330
Just a little more.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.070
We just have to get out 
while they're off-guard.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:57.880
Yae...?!

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:05.140
It hurts!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.050
Yaeko?!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.970
It hurts! It hurts!

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.180
It hurts so much!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:26.950
H-Huh?

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.200
Is this water?

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:34.330
Where did they get that ability?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.930
Alex!

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.650
Alex?!

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:08.410
Yaeko?!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.490
Alex?!

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:11.440
<i>Damn it all!</i>

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:12.760
<i>At a time like this,</i>

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:15.630
<i>where on this planet are you, 
and what are you doing?</i>

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:16.680
<i>Joe...</i>

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.420
<i>Your M.A.R.S. ranking is...</i>

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:38.870
No!

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.570
H-Huh?

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.740
How...?!

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:52.410
Don't worry.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:56.290
Your beautiful love brought me here.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.040
I made it, Michelle-san!

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.900
It's okay now.

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.780
Because Rank 1 is here!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.510
<b>Joseph G. Newton</b>

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.510
<b>Europe-Africa No. 6 Division</b>

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.510
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking 1</b>

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
Top Ranking

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:39.890
Humans shall become human soon.
